{
  "id": "MIME-72l.49",
  "title": "cert.rs and verify.rs: verify_rsa_pkcs1 and ecdsa helpers duplicated",
  "description": "verify_rsa_pkcs1, verify_ecdsa_p256, and verify_ecdsa_p384 are implemented nearly identically in both cert.rs (for cert chain validation) and verify.rs (for SignerInfo verification). The only difference is error mapping: cert.rs maps to SmimeError::CertChain, verify.rs maps to SmimeError::Io. Suggested rewrite: move the three functions to a shared internal module (e.g. crypto_verify) with a caller-supplied error mapper, or accept a closure/fn pointer for the error type. This eliminates the duplication and ensures a fix to one path (e.g. switching to a higher-level RustCrypto verify API) applies to both callers.",
